CM ============================================================
CM NEC-2 Model: Base-Loaded 5m Whip Vertical for 40m/80m
CM Document:    TM-HFTN-NEC-004
CM Author:      Merv Martin
CM Date:        2026-05-02
CM ============================================================
CM Description:
CM   5-meter whip antenna with series base loading coil.
CM   Models a short mobile/portable vertical that is electrically
CM   shortened and resonated with a lumped inductance (LD card).
CM
CM   Total height: 5.0m
CM   Loading coil: at 0.5m above base (segment 5 of vertical)
CM   Wire radius: 0.002m (vertical), 0.001m (radials)
CM   4 radials at z=0, each 5.0m long
CM
CM   40m operation: L = 15 µH at 7.15 MHz
CM     Reactance: XL = 2π × 7.15e6 × 15e-6 = 675 ohms
CM     This resonates the ~5m whip (electrically ~18 deg at 7.15 MHz)
CM
CM   80m operation: L = 60 µH at 3.65 MHz  (see FR card below)
CM     Reactance: XL = 2π × 3.65e6 × 60e-6 = 1374 ohms
CM     NOTE: Change LD card inductance for 80m evaluation.
CM
CM Ground: Sommerfeld-Norton, sigma=0.005 S/m, eps_r=13
CM Source: base of vertical (segment 1)
CM
CM Wire subdivision:
CM   Vertical: 20 segments over 5.0m = 0.25m per segment
CM   Loading coil at segment 5 (z = 1.00m to 1.25m)
CM   This places coil above ground for physical clearance.
CM
CM Coordinate system:
CM   Vertical element: x=0, y=0, z=0 to 5m
CM   Radials at z=0: 4 directions, each 5m
CM --- GEOMETRY ---
CM Wire 1: Vertical element (0 to 5m)
CM GW  tag  nseg  x1    y1    z1    x2    y2    z2    radius
CM
CM Radials (4 × 5m, z=0, 90 deg spacing)
CM Wire 2: Radial at 0 deg (+x)
CM Wire 3: Radial at 90 deg (+y)
CM Wire 4: Radial at 180 deg (-x)
CM Wire 5: Radial at 270 deg (-y)
CM
CM --- GROUND ---
CM --- LOADING (Lumped Inductance at segment 5 of wire 1) ---
CM LD  type  tag  seg  seg  R_ohms  L_henries  C_farads
CM type 0 = series RLC; R=0, C=0 (pure inductance)
CM 15 µH = 15e-6 H for 40m operation
CM --- EXCITATION ---
CM Voltage source at segment 1 (base, z=0 to z=0.25m)
CM --- FREQUENCY ---
CM Single frequency: 7.15 MHz (40m)
CM To evaluate 80m: change FR to 3.65 and LD to 60e-6
CM --- CURRENT DISTRIBUTION ---
CM --- RADIATION PATTERN ---
CM Elevation cut, theta 0-90 deg, step 2 deg
CM Azimuth cut at elevation 20 deg (theta=70)
CM ============================================================
CM LOADED VERTICAL THEORY:
CM   A 5m whip at 7.15 MHz is 5/41.96m = 0.119 lambda (43 deg).
CM   It presents a capacitive reactance at the base that must be
CM   cancelled by a series inductance for resonance.
CM
CM   Short whip base impedance (approximate):
CM     Rrad ≈ 7 × (h/lambda)^2 × 1600 = very low (~4-8 ohms)
CM     Xcap ≈ -600 to -800 ohms (highly capacitive)
CM
CM   The 15 µH loading coil (XL = 675 ohms at 7.15 MHz) provides
CM   partial resonance. Full resonance requires adjustment of L
CM   or an additional series capacitor/inductor.
CM
CM   Efficiency of loaded short verticals:
CM     η = Rrad / (Rrad + Rloss)
CM     where Rloss = coil Q loss + ground loss
CM     For Q=100 coil: Rloss_coil = XL/Q = 675/100 = 6.75 ohms
CM     Rrad (~6 ohms) → η ≈ 6/(6+6.75+5) = ~34%
CM     Use highest-Q coil possible (silver-plated, large dia, air-core)
CM
CM 40m / 80m INDUCTANCE TABLE:
CM   Freq    Target XL    L required
CM   7.15    675 ohms     15 µH   (loaded at seg 5, z=1m)
CM   3.65    1374 ohms    60 µH   (change LD card: 60.0e-6)
CM   3.50    1319 ohms    60 µH   (close enough for 80m CW end)
CM
CM MOTORIZED TUNER APPLICATION:
CM   Replace fixed coil with roller inductor (see motorized_tuner project).
CM   Stepper motor adjusts inductance 0–80 µH continuously.
CM   NEC model can be re-run at each L step to map Z(L) vs frequency.
CM   Feed into matching network (L-network or transmatch) for 50-ohm match.
CM
CM WIRE TAG REFERENCE:
CM   Wire 1: vertical (tags 1–20)
CM   Wire 2: radial 0 deg (tags 21–30)
CM   Wire 3: radial 90 deg (tags 31–40)
CM   Wire 4: radial 180 deg (tags 41–50)
CM   Wire 5: radial 270 deg (tags 51–60)
CM ============================================================
CM NOTE (2026-09-02): Radials were originally modeled flat at Z=0 (buried
CM   radial approximation), which nec2c rejects -- a segment cannot lie exactly
CM   in the ground plane under real (Sommerfeld) ground. Radials raised to
CM   Z=0.02m to clear the ground plane; electrically negligible at this scale.
CM   This is a common practical workaround, not a rigorous buried-radial model --
CM   for true buried-radial physics, use the GN cards radial ground screen
CM   parameters (NRADL/SCRWLT/SCRWRAD) instead of explicit on-ground GW wires.
